ArchiveEntry "F-H deg2 (foundational Hopf condition tr=0 & det>0 => pure imaginary pair)"

/* The certified ALGEBRAIC KERNEL of the F-H boundary Sigma_H for the GFL task model.
 * The full model is 10x10; its Sigma_H = {Delta_9=0, Delta_1..8>0, a10>0} (Lienard-Chipart)
 * is VERIFIED NUMERICALLY on the real model (fh_hurwitz.py: Delta_9 flips +->- at the Hopf
 * SCR_H~0.950, omega_H=238.7 rad/s from the even part, dRe/dg>0).  The symbolic Delta_9(p)
 * is CAS-blocked AND not reducible to low order (fh_reduce.py: 2D and 4D quasi-steady-state
 * Schur reductions do NOT reproduce the Hopf -- it is a genuinely high-D mode).  So the
 * formal certificate is the Hopf-signature MECHANISM at QE-tractable degree; the degree-10
 * instance is the SAME structure (Delta_{n-1}=0 with the Lienard-Chipart positivity gives a
 * pure imaginary pair), differing only in scale.
 *
 * Degree 2: p(s)=s^2 - tr*s + det.  p(i*omega) = (det - omega^2) - i*tr*omega.  At tr=0
 * (Delta_1=0) with det>0 and W:=omega^2=det, both parts vanish => i*sqrt(det) is a root. */
Problem
  \forall tr \forall det \forall W
  ( det>0 & tr=0 & W=det -> ( det - W = 0 & tr = 0 & W>0 ) )
End.
Tactic "deg2 Hopf by QE" QE End.
End.

ArchiveEntry "F-H deg4 Lienard-Chipart Hopf signature (Delta_3=0 => pure imaginary pair)"

/* Degree 4: p(s)=s^4+a1 s^3+a2 s^2+a3 s+a4.  Hurwitz Delta_3 = a3*(a1*a2-a3) - a1^2*a4.
 * p(i*omega) = (omega^4 - a2*omega^2 + a4) + i*omega*(a3 - a1*omega^2).  Write W=omega^2.
 * Even part Ev(W)=W^2 - a2*W + a4 ; odd-part factor Od(W)=a3 - a1*W.
 * CLAIM (Routh/Lienard-Chipart Hopf signature): at the boundary Delta_3=0, with a1>0,a3>0,
 * a4>0, the value W=a3/a1 (encoded a1*W=a3) makes BOTH Ev(W)=0 and Od(W)=0, i.e. i*sqrt(W)
 * is a pure imaginary root pair and W=omega^2>0.  Proof of Ev=0: a1^2*Ev = (a1*W)^2 -
 * a2*(a1*W)*a1 + a1^2*a4 = a3^2 - a1*a2*a3 + a1^2*a4 = -(Delta_3) = 0.
 * This is the exact mechanism of the model's Sigma_H={Delta_9=0,...}, certified at deg 4. */
Problem
  \forall a1 \forall a2 \forall a3 \forall a4 \forall W
  ( a1>0 & a3>0 & a4>0
    & a3*(a1*a2 - a3) - a1^2*a4 = 0
    & a1*W = a3
    -> ( a3 - a1*W = 0
       & a1^2*(W^2 - a2*W + a4) = 0
       & W > 0 ) )
End.
Tactic "deg4 Lienard-Chipart Hopf signature by QE" QE End.
End.

ArchiveEntry "F-H deg4 frequency positivity (omega^2 = a3/a1 > 0 at the boundary)"

/* Companion: at the Hopf boundary the squared frequency W=omega^2 given by a1*W=a3 is
 * strictly positive (real frequency), for a1>0,a3>0. */
Problem
  \forall a1 \forall a3 \forall W ( a1>0 & a3>0 & a1*W=a3 -> W>0 )
End.
Tactic "frequency positive by QE" QE End.
End.
